    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that makes sense. My concern is that these aren't just one-off errors; they seem almost intentional in how they are spaced out, like they're specifically designed to fly under the radar of the standard reconciliation. \n\nWhen we talk about these \"procedural gaps,\" how do I differentiate between simple human error—like someone forgetting a receipt—and someone actually exploiting the system to siphon off small amounts? Is there a specific red flag in the transaction metadata that usually signals something more deliberate?",
