      "content": "To distinguish between error and intentional laundering, look for metadata anomalies such as declining transaction amounts exactly at the reconciliation threshold or transactions occurring before a standard vendor upload cycle completes. Intentional gaps often feature perfect timing against checkpoints or identical amounts that refuse to add to clean totals, whereas human errors usually show varying margins and inconsistent timestamps rather than a synchronized pattern. I recommend running these flagged records through a Trend Analysis add-in that isolates deviations by day of the week to see if the spend is artificially clustered around specific operational windows when supervision is lowest.",
